# Rocdown site configuration

Place `rocdown.toml` at the documentation content root when you need site metadata,
hashed assets, or curated navigation. The file is optional: a directory of
`.rocdown` pages, or a single `.rocdown` file whose parent is the content root,
is enough for `rocdown build`, `rocdown check`, and `rocdown run`.

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- build report.rocdown --output dist
cargo run -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- run report.rocdown
```

## Example

```toml
[site]
title = "Rocci"
description = "Rocci — Composable authoring for applications and content"
base_url = "https://rocci.dev"
language = "en"
repository = "https://github.com/koliyo/rocci"
social_image = "/assets/og.png"
subtitle = "Composable authoring for applications and content"
footer = "Rocci is experimental software."

[build]
output = "../dist/rocci.dev"
assets = "assets"

[[nav]]
label = "Start here"
items = ["index", "getting-started/quickstart"]

[[nav]]
label = "Reference"
items = ["reference/rocci", "reference/rocdown"]
```

Unknown keys are errors.

## Snippets and examples

Optional snippet roots are resolved relative to the content root. They still
cannot escape the repository parent, and include paths cannot contain `..`,
NUL, or absolute locations.

```toml
[snippets]
roots = ["snippets", "../examples"]

[examples]
timeout_ms = 30000
allow_network = false
```

`@docs include` reads a file as nested Rocdown (`.rocdown`, no `@page`) or as a
code literal. Named regions use `docs-region: NAME` / `docs-region-end: NAME`
markers. Line ranges emit warning `RD2504`. Cycles are `RD2505`. Included files
are watch inputs for `rocdown run`.

`rocdown check` validates components and includes without Roc. Untested
`@docs example` records warn (`RD2601`). Example commands never run during
`rocdown build` or `rocdown check`.

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- test docs
cargo run -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- test docs --update
```

`rocdown test` runs declared `test` argument lists with cwd at the content root, a
timeout, no extra environment, and no shell expansion. `--update` rewrites
golden files. Failures are diagnostics (`RD2603`); `dist/` is not written.
Fenced code is never executed. Default CSP stays `script-src 'none'`; tab
panels are stacked sections, not a JavaScript tablist.

## Site fields

| Field | Default | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `title` | `Documentation` | Header, metadata, and generated index title |
| `description` | Empty | Default page and agent-index description |
| `base_url` | Empty | Canonical, sitemap, and absolute discovery URLs |
| `language` | `en` | Document language |
| `repository` | Empty | Source link in the header |
| `social_image` | Empty | Site-relative Open Graph image path |
| `subtitle` | Empty | Short header tagline beside the brand |
| `footer` | Empty | Article footer text |
| `csp` | Strict static default | Content-Security-Policy for generated HTML |

`base_url` must use HTTP or HTTPS. A trailing slash is normalized away.
Empty `subtitle` and `footer` omit those chrome pieces. Leave `csp` empty to use
the default policy: no scripts, no `unsafe-eval` or `unsafe-inline`, styles and
images from `'self'`.

## Build fields

`output` is resolved relative to the content root unless `--output` overrides
it. `assets` names a directory whose files are content-hashed into `/assets/`
in the published tree (`og.png` becomes `og.<hash>.png`). Markdown and `@img`
URLs under that tree are rewritten whether they are authored as
`/assets/foo.png` or `assets/foo.png`. `social_image` is rewritten the same way.

Local image paths resolve against the source file directory. Missing files fail
`rocdown check` with `RD2103`. Validated page and heading links are rewritten to
emitted routes after catalog resolve, so a passing check implies a usable href.

Rocdown writes into a staging directory and atomically replaces the output only
after a successful build.

The first-party `RocdownBase` article CSS is extracted once, hashed, and linked
from every page, including sites with a project-local `theme/`. Project chrome
and named layouts compile beside it. Generated HTML declares the CSP with a
`<meta>` tag. Article HTML must be a component body parameter; a record field
named `content` is escaped as text.

`build.theme` names a directory or `SiteShell.rocci` file relative to the
content root. When omitted, Rocdown uses `theme/` if it contains `.rocci`
files, otherwise the builtin documentation shell.

## Composable content mounts

Sites can mount external documentation catalogs or content trees using `[[mount]]` tables in `rocdown.toml`. This allows maintaining standalone documentation at repository root (`docs/`) while mounting it into a full website (`site/`):

```toml
[[mount]]
source = "../docs"
prefix = "docs"
layout = "docs"
```

- `source`: Relative path to the mounted content directory.
- `prefix`: Route and page ID prefix (e.g. `prefix = "docs"` maps `getting-started/quickstart` to ID `docs/getting-started/quickstart` and route `/docs/getting-started/quickstart/`).
- `layout`: Optional default layout applied to pages in this mount.

## Navigation

Each navigation item is a stable page ID derived from the content-root-relative
path without `.rocdown`:

| Source | Page ID | Route |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `index.rocdown` | `index` | `/` |
| `guides/index.rocdown` | `guides/index` | `/guides/` |
| `guides/build.rocdown` | `guides/build` | `/guides/build/` |

Navigation order is explicit. Unknown IDs and duplicate items fail the build.
Published pages may remain unlisted when that is intentional.

Each page also gets a right-hand “On this page” outline from heading levels 2
and 3. That rail is documentation-site chrome. A single `.rocdown` file opened
with `rocdown run` uses the standalone left navigator instead; see
[Rocdown](/docs/reference/rocdown/).

## Generated artifacts

In addition to page HTML, a configured build emits hashed `/assets/` files, a
themed `404.html`, alias redirect HTML, and `llms.txt`. When `base_url` is set,
it also emits `sitemap.xml` and `robots.txt`.

`rocdown inspect artifacts` lists the planned output tree, including hashed asset
paths, without invoking Roc.

Build this site's content from the repository root with:

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- build docs
```

Preview with watch and live reload:

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- run docs
```

`rocdown run` writes to a temp directory by default so it does not replace
`build.output`. Pass `--output` to keep the preview files. `--no-window` serves
in the browser only. Static content reloads after a successful rebuild; dynamic
islands are not part of this preview path.

## Open Knowledge Format (OKF)

Knowledge bundles are managed through the dedicated [`rocci-okf`](/docs/reference/cli/) application rather than the documentation site generator:

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-okf -- check knowledge --profile rocci
cargo run -p rocci-okf -- run knowledge
```
